B = [
('Sony','East Asia','1980s-90s','electronics','In the style of Sony, precise, miniaturised, engineered high-tech design. Compact black or silver forms with crisp bevelled edges, small softened corners and brushed aluminium faces. Dense, orderly rows of small rectangular keys, tiny green, amber and blue-green glowing readouts, and metallic blue or silver with sparing orange accents. Deep black cabinets with flat clean sides. Labels are fine, stencil-like capital sans-serif with thin embossed numbers. Later looks drift to minimal matte black slabs with thin glowing coloured light strips. Mood is technical, exact and aspirational.'),
('Technics','East Asia','1970s-80s','electronics','In the style of Technics, serious, studio-grade, quietly luxurious precision. Wide, flat, low-slung black or silver forms with thick brushed aluminium front panels, heavy rotary knobs with knurled edges and rows of slim piano-style keys. Rectangular illuminated meters with needles or segmented green and amber light bars. Glossy dark smoked acrylic covers, strobe-dot ring details and engraved scale lines. Fine neat white sans-serif lettering, rack-mount proportions and a calm horizontal emphasis. Everything feels weighty, balanced and professional.'),
('Nintendo','East Asia','1980s-present','toys','In the style of Nintendo, playful, approachable, toy-like yet neatly built. Compact rounded rectangles with chunky friendly proportions in glossy and matte plastic, white, light grey, red and black with bright primary or pastel colour accents. Controls are cross-shaped or small round coloured buttons in red, blue, yellow and green arranged in tidy symmetrical layouts. Vintage looks use cream-grey casing with dark red trim and gold lettering, later looks use clean white or black slabs with colourful detachable parts. Rounded sans-serif lettering, often in red. Cheerful and tidy.'),
('Sega','East Asia','1990s','electronics','In the style of Sega, edgy, fast, arcade-bright energy. Glossy black plastic with sharp angular wedge shapes, circular recessed details, moulded ridges and vents, and curved grips with oversized round buttons. Cobalt blue lettering and swirl marks with white and orange accents, loud saturated artwork with bold outlines and hard-edged speed lines, and glowing red or green indicator lights. A later softer variant is pale off-white and square with a gentle spiral. Typography is slanted bold italic capitals that feel futuristic and quick.'),
('Atari','North America','1970s-80s','electronics','In the style of Atari, warm, retro-futuristic 1970s den character. Heavy wedge-shaped forms clad in simulated dark woodgrain vinyl with black ribbed plastic tops, and chunky silver toggle switches lined up along an edge. Thick black controls with a single round red button on a square base. Palette is warm brown, black and silver, with painted artwork in orange, purple and teal. Logo is a three-bar fan-like mark in white or red with rounded geometric capitals. Beige-grey chunky-keyed variants exist. Cosy, bulky and optimistic.'),
('Commodore','North America','1980s','electronics','In the style of Commodore, nerdy, hobbyist, cosy 1980s home-tech character. Wide beige or brown-beige plastic with a sloped wedge profile, thick rows of chunky rectangular keys in grey and light brown with small coloured graphic symbols on their fronts, and a rainbow stripe or slim dark band across the case. Tiny red indicator lights and ribbed vent grilles. Matching cream add-on boxes and boxy dark-bezelled screens showing blue fields with light-blue borders and blocky pixel text. Logo is a bold angular chevron in stylised capitals.'),
('Olivetti','Europe','1950s-70s','electronics','In the style of Olivetti, playful, elegant, optimistic office design treated as sculpture. Soft flowing organic curves in glossy moulded plastic or pressed steel, polished to a gleaming industrial finish. Bright signal red, lemon yellow, teal and orange, with matching carry shells and smooth enamelled panels. Round-topped white keys, recessed rows of tiny coloured keys and small round dials. Lettering is lower-case or rounded sans-serif in white or black, often with a small stripe of colour on the face. Simple shapes, artisanal and joyful.'),
('Bang & Olufsen','Europe','1960s-present','electronics','In the style of Bang & Olufsen, refined, sculptural, serene Scandinavian luxury. Slender, tall, minimalist forms in brushed and polished aluminium, black glass and pale oiled wood, with thin plates that seem to float and tapered cone or pyramid volumes. Fabric grilles in charcoal or warm grey. Controls are almost invisible, hairline touch strips or a single large circular dial, with subtle white or amber displays and hidden panels that slide away. Razor-sharp edges with tiny perfectly even gaps. Palette is silver, black, natural oak, dark walnut and occasional soft earthy tones. Lettering is tiny, thin and lowercase.'),
('Leica','Europe','1930s-present','cameras','In the style of Leica, understated, crafted, timeless precision. Compact rectangular forms with a flat top plane, in black enamel or polished silver chrome, wrapped in finely pebbled black leatherette. Small window openings at the top front, knurled dials, a thin lever and a round knob on top. Lens-like barrels are slim, with fine knurled rings, engraved white and red numerals and a tiny red dot accent. Brass shows through worn paint on edges. Minimal, no clutter, with a small white script logo.'),
('Hasselblad','Europe','1950s-present','cameras','In the style of Hasselblad, serious, rugged, professional, sculptural. A cubic, square-profiled body in satin black paint with bright chrome trim, or all-black crinkle texture. Modular blocks clip together, with a large round barrel in chrome or black, coloured rings and engraved white numerals. A folding hood or angular crown on top, a side crank and one large button. Bold white capital lettering. Special editions use bright colours or exposed carbon. Heavy, exact, engineered and block-like.'),
('Polaroid','North America','1970s-80s','cameras','In the style of Polaroid, nostalgic, friendly, snapshot-casual 1970s consumer look. Bulky, sleek, boxy or folding bodies in beige, white or black plastic with a dark leatherette grip panel, a big single round lens and a bright rectangular flash bar. Chocolate-brown and tan palette with a rainbow stripe of red, orange, yellow, green and blue across the front, and a big red rectangular button. Images are square with a thick white border and a wide chin, glossy, soft warm, slightly faded colour. Bold rounded white sans-serif lettering.'),
('Nikon','East Asia','1960s-80s','cameras','In the style of Nikon, rugged, professional, mechanical. Boxy bodies with a raised angular hump on top, in black enamel or silver chrome with finely pebbled leatherette. Heavy metal knurled dials, a chunky lever and a bold yellow and black stripe accent. Barrels are black with deep rubber-ribbed rings and engraved white, orange and green numerals. Bold white capital lettering on the front of the hump. Everything feels tough, dense and made to be used hard.'),
('Canon','East Asia','1970s-80s','cameras','In the style of Canon, dependable, practical, quietly handsome. Compact boxy bodies with a black or silver top plane, wood-grain or fine black leatherette covering, and rows of tiny metal dials and small silver buttons. Clean rectangular layout with a large angular crown, a round speed dial and a thick lever. Barrels are black with subtle knurling and a red ring accent at the front for top-grade pieces. Lettering is a stylised red script mark. Tidy, well-judged and unflashy.'),
('Fujifilm','East Asia','2010s-present','cameras','In the style of Fujifilm, tactile, classic, clean and understated retro-modern design. Compact rangefinder-like bodies with a flat top plane in silver and black, matte black paint over metal and fine textured grips. Many machined aluminium dials sit on top with engraved numerals, and chunky rings with engraved scales wrap round barrels. A small offset viewing window in a corner, red ruler-like labels and neat black pebbled leatherette. Lettering is crisp white capitals. Feels hands-on, analogue and calm.'),
('Casio','East Asia','1980s-present','watches','In the style of Casio, cheap, functional, geeky and indestructible. Lightweight resin in black, grey, silver or bright primary colours with squared-off octagonal or rectangular bezels. Grey-green segmented displays with chunky digits, small rubber push buttons on the sides labelled in tiny white capitals, and tough rubberised protective surrounds. Gold-finished steel variants appear. Grid layouts of keys in grey, orange and blue. Printed text is dense, small and technical with many function labels around the face. Utilitarian and playful.'),
('Seiko','East Asia','1960s-80s','watches','In the style of Seiko, clean, practical, quietly sophisticated and slightly retro. Stainless steel with sharp faceted lugs, mixing polished and brushed surfaces under a clear domed crystal. Faces in deep blue, black, silver, champagne or sunburst green with fine radial brushing, applied baton markers filled with luminous paint, a small window at three and slim bright hands. Rotating bezels with a luminous pip and chunky bracelet links. Text is small silver capitals and a stylised sans-serif wordmark.'),
('Rolex','Europe','1950s-present','watches','In the style of Rolex, solid, imposing, polished, status-heavy Swiss luxury. Round robust cases of polished and brushed stainless steel or yellow gold with a fluted or smooth bezel, a protected screw-down crown topped with a tiny crown mark, and a magnifying bubble over the date window. Faces are glossy black, white, blue, green or champagne with applied polished markers, luminous dots and broad sword-shaped hands. Bracelets have three links with satin centres and polished outer links. Lettering is crisp small serif capitals in gold or white.'),
('Omega','Europe','1950s-70s','watches','In the style of Omega, purposeful, elegant and exploratory with a vintage space-age touch. Round steel with clean faceted lugs, polished or brushed, under a domed crystal. Black aluminium bezels with white scale numerals. Faces are matte black or silver with contrasting sub-dials, baton hands, applied markers with luminous infill, and a small Greek letter mark at twelve. Black leather straps with white stitching or tapering steel links. Lettering is crisp, slim white sans-serif.'),
('Patek Philippe','Europe','1930s-present','watches','In the style of Patek Philippe, refined, understated, heirloom and timeless haute craft. Slim round or oval cases in polished rose gold, yellow gold or platinum with elegant fine lugs, a thin bezel and a hand-stitched alligator strap in brown or black. Faces are cream, silvered or deep blue with finely guilloched texture, slender leaf-shaped hands, applied gold classical numerals or batons, and discreet small windows. Proportions are clean with discreet crowns. Typography is fine serif capitals and delicate cursive.'),
('Nomos Glashutte','Europe','1990s-present','watches','In the style of Nomos Glashutte, spare, precise, calm and modern minimalism. Slim round stainless steel with thin straight lugs, a very narrow bezel and a flat domed crystal over a pure white or silvery-white face. Slender blued steel hands, thin black numerals in a clean geometric sans-serif, a tiny subsidiary dial at six and a thin ring track. Plain brown or cordovan leather straps. Transparent backs reveal a decorated mechanism with stripes and blued screws.'),
('Junghans','Europe','1950s-70s','watches','In the style of Junghans, pared-back, functional and Bauhaus-like in discipline. Round or rectangular faces with extremely clean layouts, slim baton or simple stick hands, thin black line markers or short numerals in a geometric sans-serif, and a gently domed crystal. Cases in matte steel or gold with minimal detail. Colours are white, black and grey with occasional warm orange or yellow accent hands. Small cylinders or squares of off-white enamel or wood with tiny perforation details. Quiet and rational.'),
('Smeg','Europe','1950s-retro','appliances','In the style of Smeg, cheerful, nostalgic, boutique-fashionable retro. Curvaceous rounded rectangles in glossy pastel enamel colours such as cream, pastel blue, pink, mint green and red, with polished chrome handles, trim and rounded corners. Large thick metal rounded edges recall 1950s American cars, with a bold chrome oval mark on the front. Controls are chunky chrome knobs and rounded toggles. Surfaces are shiny and seamless with a soft sheen.'),
('KitchenAid','North America','1930s-present','appliances','In the style of KitchenAid, sturdy, generous, homey with a vintage curve. Heavy cast metal bodies with smooth bulbous curved tops, tilting heads on rear hinges and tall flat-bottomed steel or glass vessels with curved handles. Glossy enamel in empire red, onyx black, white, pistachio, pastel blue and cream, with polished chrome levers and a round hub at the front. Attachments in brushed silver. Stainless script lettering on the front.'),
('Dyson','Europe','1990s-present','appliances','In the style of Dyson, engineered, futuristic, glossy and rather industrial. Transparent clear plastic chambers reveal inner mechanics against bright coloured plastic parts in purple, fuchsia, yellow, nickel grey and iron. Parts are tubular and ribbed, with exposed engineering, smooth curved moulding, visible fixings and large chunky wheels. Thin glossy rings on tall tapering stands replace conventional shapes. Small colour-coded buttons and tiny LCD readouts. Lettering is small and bold.'),
('Bosch Professional','Europe','1990s-present','tools','In the style of Bosch Professional, robust, ergonomic, cool and professional. Hard bodies in a distinctive deep blue plastic with black rubberised soft grips and bold red logo marks. Compact shapes with ergonomic curved handles, textured diamond-pattern grips and bright silver metal parts. Labels are crisp white capital sans-serif with small red warning stickers. Battery packs are blue and black with a small LED level gauge. Cases are tough blue-grey moulded boxes with silver latches.'),
('Makita','East Asia','1990s-present','tools','In the style of Makita, solid, workmanlike and cool teal. Strong teal-blue-green plastic housings with black rubberised handles and black power packs, a red stripe on the label and tough silver or steel metalwork. Shapes are compact and rounded with chunky triggers, ribbed overmoulded grips and neat rows of small ventilation slots. Text is bold white capital lettering with a boxed brand mark. Bright yellow warning labels and small work lights.'),
('DeWalt','North America','1990s-present','tools','In the style of DeWalt, loud, rugged, jobsite-ready and high-visibility. Bright yellow plastic housings with black rubberised grips and black accent bands, boxy chunky shapes with strong ribbing and protective rubber bumpers. Power packs are chunky yellow and black blocks with a small gauge. Text is bold black block capitals on yellow with heavy outlined logo panels, and small silver steel parts. Cases are rugged yellow and black stackable boxes with big latches.'),
('Milwaukee Tool','North America','2000s-present','tools','In the style of Milwaukee Tool, aggressive, rugged, masculine and industrial. Signature bright red plastic housings with black rubberised grips and black power packs, bold stripes of red against black, tough angular shapes with big chunky triggers and reinforced rubber guards. Lettering is large white or black block capitals in a heavy italic sans-serif. Metal parts are raw silver steel. Cases combine red and black with sturdy latches.'),
('Fender','North America','1950s-60s','instruments','In the style of Fender, bright, twangy, sunny California mid-century. Sleek slab bodies with offset contours, sunburst finishes fading from yellow through red to black, or solid Surf Green, Daphne Blue, Fiesta Red and cream. White or tortoiseshell scratchplates, chrome knobs and hardware, pale maple necks with black dot markers, and a bold curved script logo. Companion cabinets have tweed or black vinyl, silver grille cloth, chrome corner trim and a row of cream or black knobs.'),
('Gibson','North America','1950s-60s','instruments','In the style of Gibson, rich, warm, heavy and luxurious. Carved arched bodies with a glossy cherry red or golden sunburst finish, cream binding around the edges and a flamed maple figure. Bold mother-of-pearl block or trapezoid inlays on dark rosewood, gold-plated hardware, chrome-covered twin pickups, gold barrel knobs and a swept-back headstock with a pearl inlay logo and crown shape.'),
('Marshall Amplification','Europe','1960s-70s','instruments','In the style of Marshall Amplification, loud, stacked, rock and roll and imposing. Large black vinyl-covered cabinets with a woven basket-weave cloth front in tan or black, trimmed with gold or silver piping and a bold white script logo on a gold or black panel at the top. Control panel with a row of chunky black skirted knobs with white numerals, a red jewel lamp and a rocker switch. Tall rectangular blocks stacked like a wall.'),
('Moog Music','North America','1970s','instruments','In the style of Moog Music, warm, vintage, scientific and handcrafted. Solid wood cabinets in dark walnut or black with a slanted control panel in black or silver, packed with chunky round knobs with white pointers, patch cords and jacks, and small rocker switches. Printed white labels in a clear sans-serif. Long keyboards with white and black keys. Colour accents are red, orange and white lines grouping sections.'),
('Roland','East Asia','1980s','instruments','In the style of Roland, techy, club-ready and boxy 1980s electronics. Dark grey or black angular metal and plastic cases with wide control surfaces, rows of tiny coloured plastic buttons in orange, red, blue and cream, slim sliders and small red LED displays. Rows of small rounded square pads in red, orange, yellow and white. Fine white lettering with grouped panel lines, wedge-like profiles and a bold stripe carrying the model name.'),
('Yamaha Synthesizers','East Asia','1980s','instruments','In the style of Yamaha Synthesizers, sleek, digital and early-electronic with soft grey and teal tones. Long slim cream-white or black plastic bodies with flat membrane buttons in grey, a small blue-green backlit LCD, slim data sliders and a full-length keyboard. Silver lettering with a minimal printed grid of function labels, rounded edge corners and a three-pronged fork-like logo. Restrained, tidy and calm.'),
('Teenage Engineering','Europe','2010s-present','instruments','In the style of Teenage Engineering, clean, geeky, graphic and playful. Flat, thin, rectangular aluminium or white plastic slabs with exact grids of small coloured rubber buttons in orange, grey and white, tiny round knobs and bright pixel displays. Orange and neon accents, silkscreened white and black technical lettering in a small monospaced sans-serif, minimal diagrams and fine line graphics. Rounded sleeves and playful pastel carry cases.'),
('Nothing','Europe','2020s-present','electronics','In the style of Nothing, stripped-back, nerdy, futuristic and quirky transparent tech. Clear see-through plastic and glass casings reveal internal components, circuit boards, screws and coils. Palette is white, black and transparent with a signature bright red dot accent. Glowing white light strips arranged in segments around key features. Typography is dot-matrix lettering with round dots forming monochrome numerals, and icons are pixelated. Edges are flat and squared with soft corners.'),
('Samsung','East Asia','2010s-present','electronics','In the style of Samsung, polished, bright, flat-glass and modern. Thin glossy glass slabs with curved edges, metallic frames in black, silver, gold and blue, vivid saturated screens and nearly invisible bezels. Separate circular lens-like details stand out in a vertical or horizontal strip. Thin brushed metal and glossy black or white panels with minimal touch controls. Graphics use rounded square icons, smooth sans-serif type and soft pastel colour gradients.'),
('Xiaomi','East Asia','2010s-present','electronics','In the style of Xiaomi, clean, affordable-minimal and friendly. Simple matte white plastic or glass shapes with softly rounded corners, an orange squared-rounded logo block and small flat circular bumps. Clean minimalist forms in white and light grey with a single glowing coloured ring light. Graphics use flat colourful icons with soft rounded corners and a friendly sans-serif font. Packaging is plain brown cardboard with a single orange square mark.'),
('Bose','North America','1980s-2000s','electronics','In the style of Bose, understated, comfortable and home-friendly. Compact, small rounded boxes and cubes in matte black or white with fabric-covered grilles, curved or tapering enclosures and small clean lettering. Plush rounded soft cushions in black or silver with thin padded bands and subtle buttons. Smooth rounded bodies with a brushed silver face and tiny buttons. Surfaces are soft matte and neutral with few visible fixings.'),
('Sonos','North America','2010s-present','electronics','In the style of Sonos, quiet, domestic, matte and minimal. Smooth matte cuboid or cylinder shapes in black or white with a perforated metal mesh wrapped around the whole body, and a flat top with a touch-sensitive strip of tiny glowing icons. Soft rounded corners, no visible screws, a small status light and a tiny mark. Long thin horizontal slabs for wide forms.'),
('Zenith Radio','North America','1930s-50s','electronics','In the style of Zenith Radio, polished, elegant and mid-century domestic. Wood cabinets with streamlined curved corners and a large round dial with an illuminated glass face in cream with black numerals. Bakelite knobs in black or ivory, tall slim fabric grilles with gold lines, chrome trim bars and rounded panels. Small curved glass fronts and rounded edges. A lightning bolt Z logo appears at the front.'),
('Philips','Europe','1930s-60s','electronics','In the style of Philips, homely, rounded and optimistic. Wooden or bakelite cabinets with rounded edges, big round glass dials with illuminated names, and pale ivory or chocolate-brown plastics. Controls are big ribbed knobs and piano-style keys. Fabric grilles with vertical gold slats and a small star and wave logo. Later pieces use bright plastic in cream, mustard and pastel with gently curved forms.'),
('Telefunken','Europe','1950s-60s','electronics','In the style of Telefunken, warm, glowing, heavy and domestic. Polished walnut or beech cabinets with rounded fronts, large illuminated glass scales with green and orange glowing eyes, and slim ivory keys across the bottom edge. Gold fabric grilles with ornamental slots, chrome-plated trim and big cream knobs. A diamond-shaped logo sits at the front. Rich wood, glowing glass and a heavy, generous presence.'),
('Grundig','Europe','1950s-60s','electronics','In the style of Grundig, solid, warm and middle-class. Wood-veneer cabinets, brushed gold or chrome piano keys, large round glass scales with illuminated tuning markers and a glowing green eye indicator, and pale cream or brown plastic knobs. Grey-green hammertone finishes, small meters and neat rows of lettered buttons. A diamond-shaped mark sits on the front. Plain, dependable and built to last, with gentle curves.'),
('Kodak','North America','1900s-80s','cameras','In the style of Kodak, cheerful, familiar and snapshot-friendly. Early forms are leather-covered boxes with a round lens and a simple window. Mid-century pieces have art deco ribs and chrome stripes, then moulded plastic in the 1970s and 1980s. Packaging uses a bold yellow, red and black colour scheme with big sans-serif lettering and a red stylised K mark. Bright yellow boxes with red panels.'),
('GoPro','North America','2010s-present','cameras','In the style of GoPro, rugged, active and outdoorsy. Small matte black or dark grey rubberised cubes with a large round glass lens on the front, a tiny screen and a few chunky buttons with white icons. Mounts are black plastic frames with chunky tabs, three-prong folding connectors, orange-yellow or blue rubber straps and thumbscrews. Cases are transparent waterproof boxes. Typography is bold white rounded sans-serif.'),
('Nokia','Europe','1990s-2000s','electronics','In the style of Nokia, tough, friendly and tactile. Chunky candy-bar forms in blue-grey, black, silver or bright interchangeable coloured plastic covers, with a small monochrome green-backlit display showing pixel text, a rounded keypad of soft rubber keys and a prominent curved key in the middle. Short stubby antennas or smooth rounded cases with a tiny speaker slot. Icons are simple pixel images with a friendly rounded font.'),
('Ericsson','Europe','1990s','electronics','In the style of Ericsson, sleek, grey and corporate. Slim grey or black forms with a flip cover, a stubby retractable antenna, a small greyish-green display and neat grids of rounded rectangular keys. Cool silver-blue finish, rounded corners and a clean oval logo. Earlier 1950s pieces had a one-piece curved bakelite body in ivory, black or red. Cool, tidy and businesslike.'),
('Motorola','North America','1980s-2000s','electronics','In the style of Motorola, bold, tech-era and metallic. The 1980s look is huge and cream-grey with a long rubbery antenna, a chunky rectangular keypad with large grey keys, a bright red-orange LED display and a heavy black handle. The 2000s look is razor-thin with a brushed aluminium finish, a flat keypad etched from a single metal sheet and a blue backlight glow. A stylised M bat-wing mark at the top.'),
('Lenovo ThinkPad','East Asia','1990s-present','computers','In the style of Lenovo ThinkPad, serious, utilitarian and corporate. Matte black soft-touch cases with square corners and a flat slab shape, a red rubber nub in the middle of a black keyboard, scooped matte black keys with white letters and a red-dot accent near the logo. Red-trimmed buttons, minimal silver trim, flat hinges and small status lights. Italic white text spells the name.'),
('Vitsoe','Europe','1960s-present','furniture','In the style of Vitsoe, calm, minimalist and timeless. Thin vertical aluminium tracks screwed to the wall with slim aluminium shelves hung from them on small pegs. Surfaces are powder-coated in white, black or light grey, or smooth plywood in pale birch, with sleek clean edges. Crisp panels in matte pale colours with narrow slots and small detailing. Everything is clean, orderly and rectilinear with thin lines and no decoration.'),
('Harley-Davidson','North America','1940s-present','motorcycles','In the style of Harley-Davidson, rumbling, rebellious open-road Americana. Heavy air-cooled V-twin forms with a low long silhouette, deep chrome plating, fat teardrop tank in gloss black, orange or deep red with a small bar-and-shield emblem and pinstripe scrolls, wide valanced fenders and a big round headlamp. Fringed black leather, tall flared bars, spoked or solid cast wheels, polished fins and chunky riveted details.'),
('Indian Motorcycle','North America','1930s-40s','motorcycles','In the style of Indian Motorcycle, rich, gleaming art deco Americana. Enormous deep valanced skirted fenders, flowing teardrop tank, glossy deep red paint with cream or gold pinstripes and hand-lettered script, chrome headlamp with a small lit ornament on the front mudguard, wide chrome bars, tan leather saddle with springs, long sweeping curves and polished engine fins. Lacquer colours such as Indian red, ivory and dark blue.'),
('Triumph Motorcycles','Europe','1960s','motorcycles','In the style of Triumph Motorcycles, nostalgic cafe racer and scrambler attitude. Compact lean silhouette, small peanut or tapered tank in bright colours such as silver, blaze yellow, red and pastel blue with a knee-pad badge and chrome side panels, polished alloy engine cases, chrome mudguards, round headlamp, twin chrome rear shock springs, ribbed black vinyl dual seat, upswept megaphone exhausts, wire spoke wheels and white pinstripes.'),
('Ducati','Europe','1990s-present','motorcycles','In the style of Ducati, fast, sculpted, muscular racing-bred Bologna look. Glossy Italian red with white or black accents, exposed tubular steel trellis frame in red, single-sided swingarm, visible cooling fins and dry clutch cover, sharply tapered full fairings with aggressive twin headlight, a short tail with a bold racing stripe, gold or black multi-spoke wheels, drilled discs and stacked underseat exhausts.'),
('Vespa','Europe','1950s-60s','scooters','In the style of Vespa, soft rounded one-piece shell forms in smooth pressed steel, wasp-waisted curves, enclosed side panels and a bulbous leg shield, headlight on the handlebar head, small wheels with a spare tucked at the side, chrome trim strips, pastel enamel paint in mint green, cream, sky blue, coral and ivory, a single curved bench seat in two-tone vinyl. Playful 1950s-60s Italian holiday charm.'),
('Lambretta','Europe','1950s-60s','scooters','In the style of Lambretta, mod-era 1960s chic with minimal curves and clean engineering. Slim angular silhouette with tubular frame, flat-sided panels and straight horizontal lines, an exposed rounded engine cover, long flat floorboard, tall narrow front shield with an integrated lamp, two-tone paint in grey, blue, cream and red, polished alloy horn cover, chrome rear rack, thin mirrors and racing stripes.'),
('Honda Super Cub','East Asia','1960s-present','motorcycles','In the style of Honda Super Cub, friendly, cheerful and utilitarian. Small step-through form with a pressed-steel spine frame, large clear plastic leg shield, rounded headlight, deep scalloped front mudguard, enclosed chain guard, flat bench seat in black vinyl, small horizontal engine with silver cases, simple round speedometer and small white or red hubs. Solid cheerful colours such as red, white, pale blue and bright yellow with simple minimal graphics.'),
('Kawasaki','East Asia','1970s-80s','motorcycles','In the style of Kawasaki, aggressive muscle-bike stance with racing-flag styling. Bold lime green paint as the signature colour, angular tank with white and black stripes, square-edged side covers, large air-cooled black finned engines, four-into-four chrome exhaust pipes, bikini or half fairings, bold sporty decals, stout forks with rubber gaiters and cast or spoke wheels. Loud, fast and show-off, bold and brash.'),
('Royal Enfield','South Asia','1950s-present','motorcycles','In the style of Royal Enfield, honest, rugged vintage British-Indian character. Rounded heavy build, deep teardrop tank in gloss black, deep green, maroon or cream with pinstripes and a circular badge with a cannon emblem, upright round chrome headlamp, a single long chrome silencer, polished alloy side engine cover with a pushrod tube, upright bars, a sprung single tan or black saddle, big mudguards and wire spoke wheels.'),
('Brough Superior','Europe','1920s-30s','motorcycles','In the style of Brough Superior, understated aristocratic racing elegance and fine craftsmanship. Hand-built, long, low, sleek silhouette, nickel-plated tank with a distinctive black-lined saddle shape, polished nickel and black enamel finish, gleaming exposed V-twin cylinders, girder front fork, slim mudguards, drop bars with copper cables, leather saddle on springs and brass instruments. Everything is slender, exacting and hand-finished and quietly rare.'),
('Moto Guzzi','Europe','1970s','motorcycles','In the style of Moto Guzzi, smooth, solid, clean lines with a long low rider stance. Big transverse 90 degree V-twin engine whose two cylinder heads stick out sideways, polished shaft drive, red frame or dark bodywork, teardrop tank in Italian red, silver, black or green with a small eagle emblem, black twin shock rear, chrome exhausts, cast wheels and a touring seat.'),
('BSA','Europe','1950s-60s','motorcycles','In the style of BSA, solid, utilitarian British classic. Sturdy profile, bright finishes in polished chrome and cherry red, black or sunshine yellow, tank badges of three rifles in a circle, rounded tanks with chrome side panels, big headlamp nacelle, valanced mudguards, bulky air-cooled engine in silver, wire wheels, upright bars and a ribbed dual seat. Honest, hardy and plain-spoken.'),
]
